{
  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "134",
  "quote": "(1.1) No landlord shall, directly or indirectly, with respect to any rental unit, collect or require or attempt to collect or require from a former tenant of the rental unit any amount of money purporting to be rent in respect of, (a) any period after the tenancy has terminated and the tenant has vacated the rental unit; or",
  "reason": "Section 134(1.1)(a) prohibits a landlord from requiring a former tenant to pay rent for any period after the tenancy has ended and the tenant has vacated the rental unit. Because this clause conflicts with Section 134(1.1)(a), it is void under Section 4(1)."
}

